a map called m is {"a": 1, "b": 2}.
a list called ks is m's keys.

For each k in ks,
  a value called v is m's "{k}",
  print "from keys: [{k}] lookup={v}".

a list called lit is ["a", "b"].
For each k2 in lit,
  a value called v2 is m's "{k2}",
  print "from literal: [{k2}] lookup={v2}".

a text called direct is "a".
a value called v3 is m's "{direct}".
print "from text var: lookup={v3}".
